//calc_bars_count = 3024 (12 years of 252 bars/year) - no need for more

//@version=6
indicator("early trend strong breakout", overlay = true, calc_bars_count = 12 * 252, max_bars_back = 500)

import drebel/DRELib/39 as drelib
import drebel/DREPerf/27 as dreperf

// ============================================================================================
// DESIGN NOTES - signal concepts (implementation-agnostic)
// --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Purpose: this block describes the IDEA and the market rationale behind every signal produced
// by this script. It is written to support an independent re-implementation: it deliberately
// avoids formulas, lookback lengths and other parameter choices of the current code, and it
// should not be treated as its specification. Recreate the concepts from the rationale below
// and re-derive the mechanics from scratch.
//
// Name decoder:
//   et      - "early trend": a composite state describing an emerging bullish trend
//   sb      - "strong breakout": a fresh price ceiling break on expanding, time-of-day aware
//             relative volume
//   rmv     - "relative measured volatility": contraction / expansion of short-term volatility
//   etc     - early trend + volatility contraction + strong breakout
//   mt      - Minervini-style trend template; mtc = the template + a volatility contraction
//   p1D     - the signal confirmed on the NEXT day by an opening-range breakout
//   WON     - William O'Neil inspired setups; hp = high percentile; 1YH = fresh one-year high
//   vip     - volume institutional push
//   CapLow  - capitulation low; FlatB = flat-base breakout
//   The digits 1/2/3 (rmv1..3, etc1sb..3sb, mtc1sb..3sb) are NOT a priority. They are the same
//   concept measured on different horizons: 1 = very short (fast, noisy), 2 = short (swing),
//   3 = medium (base / position level). Treat them as interchangeable alternative triggers.
//
// How the signals relate:
//   - Every signal is an independent, standalone long trigger; they are not meant to be AND-ed
//     with each other. Confluence is expressed through the shared building blocks below.
//   - What is plotted and alerted is additionally gated by the historical quality check (see
//     "Signal quality model" below): in the default mode only signals whose statistics pass the
//     configured gates are surfaced. The script is a research lab for a given instrument, not
//     just a chart overlay.
//
// --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// SHARED BUILDING BLOCKS
// --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
// 1) Universe / general filter
//    A tradeable long candidate must be a stock (not an ETF or index), with sufficient
//    liquidity (average and median turnover above a floor, so a position can be entered and
//    exited), sufficient volatility (average daily range above a floor - a signal needs
//    something to move), the price inside a sane band, and the price must not sit too far above
//    the day's low at the moment of the signal (the entry must not chase an already extended
//    intraday move; the distance is measured in units of the average daily range). In addition,
//    the broad benchmark must not be in a fresh bearish trend state.
//
// 2) Regime modifier (broad index + sector index)
//    The state of the broad market index and of the matching sector index (each classified as
//    recently bullish / recently bearish / neutral) yields a small integer modifier. It makes
//    the environment-adaptive parts of the script slightly looser in a bullish regime and
//    slightly stricter in a bearish one: the breakout volume requirement, the allowed distance
//    from the day's low, and the earnings requirement of the trend template (waived when the
//    environment is already strongly bullish). Weak market structure (too few meaningful swings
//    in the recent window) tightens the breakout volume requirement as well. Conceptually: the
//    same setup deserves a different amount of confirmation depending on the tape.
//
// 3) Strong breakout (the "sb" building block)
//    A breakout is a close above the recent price ceiling. "Strong" adds three ideas on top of
//    the bare new-high condition:
//      - multi-horizon freshness: the ceiling is measured over several nested horizons (the base
//        lookback and its multiples), and the break must be fresh - the same ceiling must not
//        have been broken already in the immediately preceding bars - so the signal marks the
//        start of an expansion, not a continuation of an old one;
//      - time-of-day aware relative volume: volume is compared to its recent average and scaled
//        by how much of the session has elapsed, because raw volume early in the day is
//        naturally low. The required multiple is high at the open and decays towards the close,
//        so a move late in the session needs less relative volume to be credible. This
//        distinguishes an intraday spike from a close-validated breakout;
//      - price above the VWAP anchored at the most recent local high: the breakout must reclaim
//        the average price paid by everyone who traded around the recent top - a genuine change
//        of control, not a bounce below supply.
//
// 4) Volatility contraction / expansion (the "rmv" building block)
//    Volatility is cyclical: quiet contracting phases (bases) precede directional expansion.
//    "Measured volatility" is the typical short-term candle range. "Contraction" means this
//    measure sits at the low end of its OWN recent range - a relative, self-normalized level,
//    not an absolute threshold, so it works across instruments. The bullish event is the moment
//    contraction ends and volatility expands again, typically confirmed by: price turning up
//    versus the recent bars, volume above its average, price back above short-term averages,
//    and the expansion happening late in the session so that the close validates it. The
//    contraction measure is also used on its own as a state filter (see etc / mtc signals).
//
// 5) Signal quality model (DREPerf library)
//    Every signal is continuously validated against the history of the instrument on the chart.
//    Outcome model: entry at the close of the signal candle; stop placed under the most recent
//    short-term lows but never risking more than a capped percentage (the higher of the two
//    levels is used); "success" = the price does not violate the stop within the check window;
//    "failure" = the stop is hit and the trade is accounted with the stop-loss return. Metrics:
//    success rate (no stop hit), mixed average return per signal, win rate, Wilson score lower
//    bound of the win rate (sample-size aware reliability), R-multiple statistics (average,
//    median, standard deviation, profit factor), average favorable and adverse excursion,
//    maximum drawdown of the signal equity curve in R, longest losing streak, and a
//    sample-aware score. The quality gate passes only when the success-rate and average-return
//    thresholds are met AND the completed sample is large enough AND the Wilson lower bound
//    clears its threshold. The minimum average return is expressed as a multiple of the
//    instrument's average daily range, so the bar scales with the instrument's volatility.
//
// --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// SIGNALS
// --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
// et3sb / et4sb - early trend + strong breakout
//   Idea: catch a stock in the earliest phase of a new uptrend, right as it breaks out. The
//   "early trend" is a composite of four independent descriptions of a trend; the signal
//   requires either all four (et4) or at least three of four (et3), combined with the strong
//   breakout:
//     - relative strength: the stock outperforms the broad benchmark - its relative-strength
//       line against the benchmark is above its own average, so the outperformance is a trend,
//       not noise;
//     - volume flow: the cumulative on-balance volume sits decisively above its own recent norm
//       (accumulation), with hysteresis so the state does not flip on single bars;
//     - trend filter: price above the Ichimoku cloud (an established, smoothed trend / momentum
//       state);
//     - market structure: within the recent window the lows hold better than the highs do - the
//       sequence of lows is not being broken while overhead highs are being absorbed (a rising
//       staircase), with a minimum amount of overall structure so pure chop does not qualify.
//   The 3-of-4 version tolerates one missing descriptor (e.g. structure already repaired while
//   volume flow has not confirmed yet); the 4-of-4 version demands full agreement.
//
// et1YHsb - early trend + fresh one-year leadership extreme + strong breakout
//   Idea: the early-trend composite has been true recently, and the stock demonstrates
//   leadership with a fresh one-year high in its volume flow (OBV) or in its relative-strength
//   line, while breaking out strongly now. The freshness of the leadership extreme is the
//   point: a stock that has just printed a yearly high in OBV or RS while a breakout starts is
//   a potential new leader, unlike a stock whose leadership is old.
//
// rmv1 / rmv2 / rmv3 - expansion out of a volatility contraction
//   Idea: see the "rmv" building block above. The bullish signal fires when the contraction
//   state ends and volatility expands, or when an extreme expansion follows a contraction
//   within a couple of bars (an explosive move right out of a quiet base). It is confirmed by
//   price turning up, relative volume, price above short-term averages and a late-session
//   timing so the close validates the expansion. Variants 1/2/3 are the same concept on very
//   short / short / medium horizons (fast and noisy vs. slow and structural).
//
// etc1sb / etc2sb / etc3sb - early trend + contraction + strong breakout
//   Idea: a stock that is already in an early uptrend (et3sb or et4sb) and is breaking out
//   strongly while its short-term volatility sits at the low end of its own range - the classic
//   quiet base under a breakout. The contraction is required either as a state (volatility
//   still compressed) or as a fresh expansion event (see rmv). Variants 1/2/3 measure the
//   contraction on three horizons.
//
// obvDiv - positive OBV / price divergence + strong breakout
//   Idea: stealth accumulation. Volume flow (OBV) is trending up while price is not - buyers
//   keep absorbing supply without the price moving yet. A sustained count of such divergence
//   bars followed by a strong breakout suggests the accumulated position is being marked up.
//
// mtsb / mtc1sb / mtc2sb / mtc3sb - Minervini-style trend + strong breakout
//   Idea: trade breakouts only in stocks that already satisfy a growth-leadership trend
//   template: price above the key averages, the averages stacked in bullish order, the
//   long-term average rising, price well above the yearly low and near the yearly high,
//   outperformance versus the benchmark, and improving earnings (the trend must be backed by
//   results; this requirement is waived when the market regime is strongly bullish). The
//   template state must be fresh (it held recently), not historical. mtsb = template + strong
//   breakout. mtc1sb/2sb/3sb = the same plus a volatility contraction on one of three horizons
//   (a quiet base under the breakout of a leader).
//
// rag-pb - runaway gap pullback
//   Idea: a "runaway gap" - the entire candle, including its low, opens and trades above the
//   previous high by more than a multiple of the average daily range, on above-average volume -
//   is an institutional footprint (someone is in a hurry). The stock then pulls back, returns
//   to the low of the gap day and defends it (touch-and-go of the gap low) while the short-term
//   trend is still up. Entry is the reclaim of the gap-day low after the pullback: buying the
//   retest of the footprint level.
//
// WON:hp-sb - O'Neil inspired: high-percentile leadership + strong breakout
//   Idea: CANSLIM-style leadership expressed as percentile ranks - volume flow (OBV), relative
//   strength versus the benchmark and earnings (EPS) all sit at high percentiles of their own
//   history, and the high-percentile state is fresh. Earnings are actually being updated
//   (recent reporting activity). Combined with a volatility contraction and a strong breakout:
//   buy the breakout of a stock that leads on all three fronts (price, volume flow,
//   fundamentals).
//
// WON:turnUp - O'Neil inspired: turnaround GO
//   Idea: a bottom-turning signal (originally for broad indexes, it also works on big stocks).
//   A recent low is confirmed - it is the extreme of a wider window too, it occurred within a
//   short window of time and below the main average, i.e. a real correction, not a shallow
//   wiggle - and then a sequence of "GO days" appears: up days on expanding volume (the
//   accumulation days of a rally attempt). A minimum number of GO days after a confirmed
//   bottom is the "follow-through" that marks a turnaround. The signal is debounced, so one
//   turnaround produces one signal.
//
// ridingVwapTAG - riding anchored VWAP: touch and go
//   Idea: anchored VWAPs as the market's memory of the average price paid since a meaningful
//   low. Starting from the major low of the recent past, every new local low below the previous
//   anchored VWAP starts a new anchor - a ladder of cost-basis levels, each defended by a
//   different cohort of buyers. The signal fires when price touches and reclaims one of these
//   levels (touch-and-go) while the structure stays clean: few violations below the level, only
//   the most recent / single level in play (not a late-stage pile-up of simultaneous levels),
//   a volume flush at the low (capitulation-style selling absorbed), price back above
//   short-term references, the main average rising, and optionally a contraction in place.
//   Confirmation: a close above the previous bar's high. Conceptually: institutions defend
//   their average price; buying the successful defense means joining the trend early.
//
// CapLow - capitulation low
//   Idea: the classic selling climax. The lowest price of a long window is printed on climax
//   volume (extreme volume percentile) - capitulation, all remaining sellers are flushed. The
//   entry is not on the climax bar itself but on the confirmation day: price holds above the
//   climax low, volume stays above average and, optionally, the day shows strength against the
//   climax bar (high above the previous high / close recovering a meaningful part of the
//   previous bar). The alert is emitted only near the end of the session, so the confirmation
//   is close-validated.
//
// FlatB - flat-base breakout
//   Idea: a breakout from a flat consolidation. For a while the price ceiling is completely
//   flat (no new highs for several bars), then the closing price jumps to the very top of its
//   long-term range in one step (the percentile rank of the close jumps to the maximum).
//   Volume must be good (the same time-of-day aware relative volume as the strong breakout),
//   and the stock must not be overextended above its main average (a low percentile of the
//   distance to the average), so the breakout comes from rest, not from an already stretched
//   move.
//
// vip - volume institutional push
//   Idea: accumulation shows up as a cluster of "accumulation days": days with above-average
//   volume and a close not lower than the previous close. Four such days in a row, or five out
//   of six, mean institutions have been pushing for a week - a footprint, not a single event.
//   The signal must be fresh (not a repetition of a recent cluster), optionally at least one of
//   the days must carry very high volume (a real institutional print), and the stock must not
//   already be at the top of its range - accumulation happens before the breakout, not after.
//
// Qul:EP2 / Qul:EP3 - Qullamaggie Episodic Pivot (EP)
//   Idea: an unexpected positive catalyst (earnings/guidance, FDA, contract, theme) produces a gap
//   up on heavy volume out of a base, not in a downtrend. Daily proxy: gap >= 10% (EP2) or 8% (EP3),
//   relative volume >= 2x (EP2) or 1.5x (EP3), close above the prior 50-day high (EP2)
//   or 20-day high (EP3), close above SMA50/SMA200 with SMA50 rising. EP2 requires a green
//   close; EP3 drops it and instead requires the gap day to close in the top 10% of its range.
//   Stop is the ETSB convention (2-day low / 8% cap). The two rows are the same epCalc logic
//   with two parameter sets: EP2 = v2 (10%, 2x, 0.50, base 50, green), EP3 =
//   c09_v15_g8_b20_greenOff (8%, 1.5x, 0.90, base 20, no green requirement). The EP3 variant is
//   named Qul:EP3 because Qul:EP2 is already taken by the v2 set.
//   Volume is time-of-day projected like strongBreakout: the full-day requirement is projected
//   from the elapsed session (early threshold = 2x the day-end threshold) and the raw full-day
//   volume remains a fallback. On closed bars this reduces to the original full-day condition,
//   so the historical table is unchanged; on the live bar the alert can fire before the close.
//
// Qul:HTF / Qul:HTF2 - Qullamaggie High Tight Flag (HTF)
//   Idea: a large prior advance (the pole), then a tight flag / pullback with higher lows and a
//   contracting range, followed by a fresh breakout on expanding volume. Daily HTF is the
//   Qullamaggie "high tight flag": pole >= 50% over at least 5 sessions, flag 10 sessions,
//   peak-to-trough pullback <= 25% and flag range <= 25%, close > SMA10 > SMA20 > SMA50 with
//   SMA50 rising, and a breakout close above the flag high on volume > 1.5x SMA50 with the
//   close in the upper half of the bar. Stop is the ETSB convention (2-day low / 8% cap).
//   Qul:HTF  = i2_margin3:      breakout margin 3%, pullback 25%.
//   Qul:HTF2 = i2_margin1_pb33: breakout margin 1%, pullback 33%.
//   Both rows call the same simplified htfCalc with five parameters: breakout margin, max
//   pullback, max base range, close-pivot switch and minimum close location. The pole threshold
//   (>=50%, >=5 sessions), tight/higher-lows, MA alignment and breakout volume (>1.5x SMA50)
//   are hardcoded; the optional dry-up, risk/ADR, 52-week-high, RS, regime, extension, gap,
//   confirmation, liquidity/price/ADR, RMV and pole-slope filters are not part of this factory.
//   Note: iteration 2 of the research sweep used closeLoc = 1.0 on zero-range bars; this port
//   follows the current ETSB convention (closeLoc = 0.0), so the historical I2 statistics may
//   differ slightly on limit-up / halted sessions. The outcome/quality model is also the ETSB
//   one (2-day low / 8% cap), so win%/avgR/score are not directly comparable with the HTF
//   research table, which used a 5-day-low stop.
//
// p1D variants (opening-range breakout on the day after the signal)
//   Idea (Qullamaggie inspired): a main signal is often only an alert; the actual entry can be
//   deferred to the next session and taken only if the stock confirms by breaking its opening
//   range (price closes at the session high after the opening range has formed, opening above
//   the previous close, within the first half of the session). For less liquid stocks the
//   opening range is measured over a longer initial window, for liquid ones over a shorter one
//   - the noise of the first minutes differs with turnover. Each signal family has its own
//   next-day variant; the aggregate "best LONG" alert fires for any of them.
//
// --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// LIBRARY PROVENANCE (for re-implementation)
// --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Part of the logic lives in two shared libraries and must be recreated as independent modules:
//   - DRELib: benchmark and sector-index selection and regime classification, the trend
//     template (Minervini-style, including the earnings component), Ichimoku cloud state,
//     OBV-above-norm state with hysteresis, the non-broken-extremes structure measure, relative
//     measured volatility (rmv), the strong breakout (multi-horizon fresh highs + time-of-day
//     aware relative volume + anchored-VWAP condition), the opening-range breakout, the O'Neil
//     turnaround GO signal, the general universe filter and the time-of-session percentage.
//   - DREPerf: the signal quality / statistics model (outcome model, success rate, mixed
//     return, win rate, Wilson lower bound, R-multiple statistics, excursions, drawdown,
//     score, quality gate).
// ============================================================================================

//common filters inputs
iGeneralFilterCond = input.bool(defval = true, title = 'Filter ON', display = display.none, group = 'General filter for signal')
iMinTurnover = input.float(defval = 0.20, title = 'Min. Turnover[M]', minval = 0.2, display = display.none, group = 'General filter for signal')
iMinAdr = input.float(defval = 3, title = 'Min. ADR[%]', minval = 0, step = 0.2, display = display.none, group = 'General filter for signal')
iMinPrice = input.float(defval = 1.0, title = 'Min.-max. price', minval = 0, display = display.none, inline = 'min max price', group = 'General filter for signal')
iMaxPrice = input.float(defval = 1750.0, title = '-', minval = 0, display = display.none, inline = 'min max price', group = 'General filter for signal')
iMaxDistFromLoDPct = input.int(defval = 67, title = 'Max. distance from LoD [%]', minval = 0, maxval = 300, step = 5, display = display.none, group = 'General filter for signal')
iMinBenchmarkNotBearishSince = input.int(defval = 31, title = 'Min. days from benchmark bearish', minval = 0, maxval = 63, display = display.none, group = 'General filter for signal')

//sig success rate filter
iShowEt3sbSig = input.bool(defval = true, title = 'Show et3sb', display = display.none, group = 'Signals')
iShowEt4sbSig = input.bool(defval = true, title = 'Show et4sb', display = display.none, group = 'Signals')
iShowEt1YHsbSig = input.bool(defval = true, title = 'Show et1YHsb', display = display.none, group = 'Signals')
iShowRmv1Sig = input.bool(defval = true, title = 'Show rmv', display = display.none, group = 'Signals', inline = "rmv")
iShowRmv2Sig = input.bool(defval = true, title = '2', display = display.none, group = 'Signals', inline = "rmv")
iShowRmv3Sig = input.bool(defval = true, title = '3', display = display.none, group = 'Signals', inline = "rmv")
iShowEtc1sbSig = input.bool(defval = true, title = 'Show etcsb', display = display.none, group = 'Signals', inline = "etcsb")
iShowEtc2sbSig = input.bool(defval = true, title = 'c2', display = display.none, group = 'Signals', inline = "etcsb")
iShowEtc3sbSig = input.bool(defval = true, title = 'c3', display = display.none, group = 'Signals', inline = "etcsb")
iShowObvDivSig = input.bool(defval = true, title = 'Show Obv-Div-sb', display = display.none, group = 'Signals')
iShowMinevriniTrendSig = input.bool(defval = true, title = 'Show MinevriniTrend-contr-sb', display = display.none, group = 'Signals', inline = "mtsb")
iShowMinevriniTrendC1Sig = input.bool(defval = true, title = 'c1', display = display.none, group = 'Signals', inline = "mtsb")
iShowMinevriniTrendC2Sig = input.bool(defval = true, title = 'c2', display = display.none, group = 'Signals', inline = "mtsb")
iShowMinevriniTrendC3Sig = input.bool(defval = true, title = 'c3', display = display.none, group = 'Signals', inline = "mtsb")
iShowRagPb = input.bool(defval = true, title = 'Show RAG-pb', display = display.none, group = 'Signals')
iShowWONHP = input.bool(defval = true, title = "Show O''Neil Inspired: hi-percentiles", display = display.none, group = 'Signals')
iShowWONTurnaroundGo = input.bool(defval = true, title = "Show O''Neil Inspired: turnaround GO", display = display.none, group = 'Signals')
iShowRidingVwap = input.bool(defval = true, title = "Show Riding Vwap TouchAndGo", display = display.none, group = 'Signals')
iShowRidingVwapDebug = input.bool(defval = false, title = "Show Riding Vwap TouchAndGo - debug", display = display.none, group = 'Signals')
iShowCapitulationLow = input.bool(defval = true, title = "Show Capitulation Low", display = display.none, group = 'Signals')
iShowFlatBreakout = input.bool(defval = true, title = "Show FlatBreakout", display = display.none, group = 'Signals')
iShowVIP = input.bool(defval = true, title = "Show Volume Institutional Push", display = display.none, group = 'Signals')
iShowQulEp2 = input.bool(defval = true, title = 'Show Qul:EP2', display = display.none, group = 'Signals')
iShowQulEp3 = input.bool(defval = true, title = 'Show Qul:EP3', display = display.none, group = 'Signals')
iShowQulHtf = input.bool(defval = true, title = 'Show Qul:HTF', display = display.none, group = 'Signals')
iShowQulHtf2 = input.bool(defval = true, title = 'Show Qul:HTF2', display = display.none, group = 'Signals')

iSigCheckTime = input.int(defval = 30, title = 'Signal check time [candles]', minval = 5, maxval = 200, display = display.none, group = 'Signals')
iSigStopLossDay = input.int(defval = 2, title = 'Stop loss (day of low)', minval = 0, maxval = 10, display = display.none, group = 'Signals')
iSigStopLossMaxPct = input.float(defval = 8.0, title = 'Stop loss [pct]', minval = 0.0, maxval = 20.0, step = 0.5, display = display.none, group = 'Signals')
iMinSigSuccessRate = input.float(defval = 46.0, title = 'Min. sig success rate [pct]', minval = 0.0, maxval = 100.0, step = 1.0, display = display.none, group = 'Signals')
iMinSigReturnAdrMultiple = input.float(defval = 1.2, title = 'Min. avg. return by ADR multiple', minval = -1.0, maxval = 5.0, step = 0.05, display = display.none, group = 'Signals')

//common filters calculations 
int sigMod = drelib.getWideIndexAndSectorSignalMod(iMinBenchmarkNotBearishSince)
bool generalFilter = drelib.generalFilter(iMinTurnover, iMinAdr, iMinPrice, iMaxPrice, 30, iMaxDistFromLoDPct, sigMod)
bool gFilter = generalFilter and iGeneralFilterCond or not iGeneralFilterCond

adrPct = 100.0 * (ta.sma(high / low, 100) - 1)
adrCond = iMinSigReturnAdrMultiple * adrPct

var int et1YHRecency = 15
var series float benchIdx = drelib.getDefaultBenchmarkClose()
rs = close / benchIdx
rs1YHigh = rs == ta.highest(rs, drelib.getDefaultStockTradingDaysInAYear())
rs1YHighLately = ta.barssince(rs1YHigh) < et1YHRecency
rsMa = ta.sma(rs, 100)
rsCondRaw = rs > rsMa
rsCond_10 = rsCondRaw ? 1 : 0

obvCondRaw = drelib.isAboveObvSmaStddev(100, 0.35)
obv1YHigh = ta.obv == ta.highest(ta.obv, drelib.getDefaultStockTradingDaysInAYear())
obv1YHighLately = ta.barssince(obv1YHigh) < et1YHRecency
obvCond_10 = obvCondRaw ? 1 : 0

[nonBrokenLowsPct, nonBrokenHighsPct, nonBrokenExtremesPct, lowsHighsRatio] = drelib.nonBrokenExtremesPct(100)
nbeCondRaw = nonBrokenLowsPct > nonBrokenHighsPct and nonBrokenExtremesPct >= 10
nbeCond_10 = nbeCondRaw ? 1 : 0

iBreakoutLookback = input.int(defval = 7, title = 'Min. breakout lookback', minval = 1, maxval = 21, display = display.none, group = 'Breakout params')
iBreakoutMultiples = input.bool(defval = true, title = 'Use also multiples of lookback', display = display.none, group = 'Breakout params')
iInitialMinVolumePct = input.int(defval = 600, title = 'Initial min. relative volume Pct.', minval = 100, display = display.none, group = 'Breakout params')
iDayEndMinVolumePct = input.int(defval = 125, title = 'Day end min. relative volume Pct.', minval = 100, display = display.none, group = 'Breakout params')

sigMod += nonBrokenExtremesPct <= 14 ? -1 : 0
strongBreakout = drelib.strongBreakout(iBreakoutLookback, iBreakoutMultiples, iInitialMinVolumePct, iDayEndMinVolumePct, sigMod, true)

aboveIchimokuCloudCondRaw = drelib.isAboveIchimokuCloud()
aboveIchimokuCloudCond_10 = aboveIchimokuCloudCondRaw ? 1 : 0

totalCond = 4
etCondSum = rsCond_10 + obvCond_10 + aboveIchimokuCloudCond_10 + nbeCond_10
et3 = etCondSum == totalCond - 1
et4 = etCondSum == totalCond
et = etCondSum >= totalCond - 1
et3sb = et3 and strongBreakout
et4sb = et4 and strongBreakout
etsb = et3sb or et4sb
etLately = ta.barssince(not et) < et1YHRecency
et1YHsb = etLately and (obv1YHighLately or rs1YHighLately) and strongBreakout

//Qullamaggie inspired - additional signal if there is an OpeningRangeBrakeout the next day after main signal
//for low turnover 60 minute orb, for mid-high turnover 5 minute orb
minTurnoverForOrb5 = drelib.minTurnoverOk(10 * iMinTurnover, 30)
orb5 = drelib.openingRangeBreakout(5, true, true)
orb60 = drelib.openingRangeBreakout(60, true, true)
orb = minTurnoverForOrb5 ? orb5 : orb60

//pct time since session beginning 
dttTime = drelib.dttTimePct()
sessionCloseToEnd = dttTime >= 90
sessionClosed = dttTime >= 1

//rmv sig (like in "DRE parabolic top" v444)
iRmvMinVolumeMultiple = input.float(defval = 1.15, title = 'Rmv volume multiple', minval = 0.0, maxval = 3.0, step = 0.05, display = display.none, group = 'Contraction (RMV)')

iContr1RmvMainLookback = input.int(defval = 13, title = 'Lookbacks (main/s1/s2/s3)', minval = 8, maxval = 200, display = display.none, inline = 'rmv lookbacks', group = 'Contraction (RMV) params 1 (v. short)')
iContr1RmvS1Lookback = input.int(defval = 5, title = '', minval = 1, maxval = 50, display = display.none, inline = 'rmv lookbacks', group = 'Contraction (RMV) params 1 (v. short)')
iContr1RmvS2Lookback = input.int(defval = 3, title = '', minval = 1, maxval = 50, display = display.none, inline = 'rmv lookbacks', group = 'Contraction (RMV) params 1 (v. short)')
iContr1RmvS3Lookback = input.int(defval = 2, title = '', minval = 1, maxval = 50, display = display.none, inline = 'rmv lookbacks', group = 'Contraction (RMV) params 1 (v. short)')
iContr1MaxBarsSinceContraction = input.int(defval = 2, title = 'Max. bars since contraction', minval = 0, display = display.none, group = 'Contraction (RMV) params 1 (v. short)')

iContr2RmvMainLookback = input.int(defval = 21, title = 'Lookbacks (main/s1/s2/s3)', minval = 10, maxval = 200, display = display.none, inline = 'rmv lookbacks', group = 'Contraction (RMV) params 2 (short)')
iContr2RmvS1Lookback = input.int(defval = 8, title = '', minval = 1, maxval = 50, display = display.none, inline = 'rmv lookbacks', group = 'Contraction (RMV) params 2 (short)')
iContr2RmvS2Lookback = input.int(defval = 5, title = '', minval = 1, maxval = 50, display = display.none, inline = 'rmv lookbacks', group = 'Contraction (RMV) params 2 (short)')
iContr2RmvS3Lookback = input.int(defval = 3, title = '', minval = 1, maxval = 50, display = display.none, inline = 'rmv lookbacks', group = 'Contraction (RMV) params 2 (short)')
iContr2MaxBarsSinceContraction = input.int(defval = 3, title = 'Max. bars since contraction', minval = 0, display = display.none, group = 'Contraction (RMV) params 2 (short)')

iContr3RmvMainLookback = input.int(defval = 55, title = 'Lookbacks (main/s1/s2/s3)', minval = 10, maxval = 200, display = display.none, inline = 'rmv lookbacks', group = 'Contraction (RMV) params 3 (medium)')
iContr3RmvS1Lookback = input.int(defval = 34, title = '', minval = 1, maxval = 50, inline = 'rmv lookbacks', display = display.none, group = 'Contraction (RMV) params 3 (medium)')
iContr3RmvS2Lookback = input.int(defval = 21, title = '', minval = 1, maxval = 50, inline = 'rmv lookbacks', display = display.none, group = 'Contraction (RMV) params 3 (medium)')
iContr3RmvS3Lookback = input.int(defval = 13, title = '', minval = 1, maxval = 50, inline = 'rmv lookbacks', display = display.none, group = 'Contraction (RMV) params 3 (medium)')
iContr3MaxBarsSinceContraction = input.int(defval = 5, title = 'Max. bars since contraction', minval = 0, display = display.none, group = 'Contraction (RMV) params 3 (medium)')

shortMa = ta.sma(close, 50)
mainMa = ta.sma(close, 200)
gVShortMa1 = ta.ema(close, 10)
gVolMa = ta.sma(volume, 30)
gVol50Ma = ta.sma(volume, 50)
rmvLowLevel = 25
otherRmvCond = close > close[2] and volume > iRmvMinVolumeMultiple * gVolMa and close > gVShortMa1 and close > shortMa and dttTime > 0.85

rmvContraction1 = drelib.rmv(iContr1RmvMainLookback, iContr1RmvS1Lookback, iContr1RmvS2Lookback, iContr1RmvS3Lookback)
lowRmv1 = rmvContraction1 <= rmvLowLevel
highRmv1 = rmvContraction1 >= 100 - rmvLowLevel / 2
rmv1Cond = not lowRmv1 and lowRmv1[1] or highRmv1 and lowRmv1[2] or rmvContraction1 == 100 and lowRmv1[3]
bullishRmv1 = rmv1Cond and otherRmvCond

rmvContraction2 = drelib.rmv(iContr2RmvMainLookback, iContr2RmvS1Lookback, iContr2RmvS2Lookback, iContr2RmvS3Lookback)
lowRmv2 = rmvContraction2 <= rmvLowLevel
highRmv2 = rmvContraction2 >= 100 - rmvLowLevel / 2
rmv2Cond = not lowRmv2 and lowRmv2[1] or highRmv2 and lowRmv2[2] or rmvContraction2 == 100 and lowRmv2[3]
bullishRmv2 = rmv2Cond and otherRmvCond

rmvContraction3 = drelib.rmv(iContr3RmvMainLookback, iContr3RmvS1Lookback, iContr3RmvS2Lookback, iContr3RmvS3Lookback)
lowRmv3 = rmvContraction3 <= rmvLowLevel
highRmv3 = rmvContraction3 >= 100 - rmvLowLevel / 2
rmv3Cond = not lowRmv3 and lowRmv3[1] or highRmv3 and lowRmv3[2] or rmvContraction3 == 100 and lowRmv3[3]
bullishRmv3 = rmv3Cond and otherRmvCond


etc1sb = etsb and (rmv1Cond or lowRmv1)
etc2sb = etsb and (rmv2Cond or lowRmv2)
etc3sb = etsb and (rmv3Cond or lowRmv3)

iDivergence = input.int(30, title = 'Min. obv-price div. pct', minval = 0, maxval = 100, display = display.none, group = 'Signal: Obv-price divergence sb')
obvMa = ta.sma(ta.obv, 100)
priceMa = ta.sma(close, 100)
risingObv = obvMa > obvMa[1]
risingPrice = priceMa > priceMa[1]
divergence = risingObv and not risingPrice
divergenceSum = math.sum(divergence ? 1 : 0, 100)
obvDiv = divergenceSum > iDivergence and strongBreakout

//minevrini trend /contraction/ strong breakout
iIncludeEarnings = input.bool(defval = true, title = 'Include earnings', display = display.none, group = 'Signal: Minevrini trend /contraction/ strong breakout')
iBetterEarningsRate = input.float(defval = 0.5, title = 'Min. earnings change rate', minval = 0.0, maxval = 1.0, step = 0.1, display = display.none, group = 'Signal: Minevrini trend /contraction/ strong breakout')

doIncludeEarnings = sigMod >= 1 ? false : iIncludeEarnings
bool minevriniTrend = drelib.isMinevriniBullishTrend(true, doIncludeEarnings, iBetterEarningsRate)

minevriniTrendCond = ta.barssince(minevriniTrend) < 63

mtsb = minevriniTrendCond and strongBreakout
mtc1sb = minevriniTrendCond and (rmv1Cond or lowRmv1) and strongBreakout
mtc2sb = minevriniTrendCond and (rmv2Cond or lowRmv2) and strongBreakout
mtc3sb = minevriniTrendCond and (rmv3Cond or lowRmv3) and strongBreakout

//RunAwayGap-pullback
iBullishRagPbMaxTimeSinceRag = input.int(defval = 50, title = 'Max. pullback time', minval = 2, maxval = 60, display = display.none, group = 'Signal: RunAwayGap - pullback')
iBullishRagPbAdrMultiple = input.float(defval = 1.5, title = 'Gap Min. Adr Multiple', minval = 0.5, maxval = 3.0, step = 0.1, display = display.none, group = 'Signal: RunAwayGap - pullback')
runAwayGap = low > high[1] + iBullishRagPbAdrMultiple * adrPct / 100 * high[1] and volume > gVolMa
runAwayGapAgo = ta.barssince(runAwayGap)
ragPb = not runAwayGap and runAwayGapAgo < iBullishRagPbMaxTimeSinceRag and drelib.crossover(low[runAwayGapAgo]) and shortMa > shortMa[1]

//William O''Neil Inspired: hi-percentile - strong breakout
countChanges(series, length) =>
    math.sum(series != series[1] ? 1 : 0, length)

iOneilPercentileLookback = input.int(200, title = 'Main percentile lookback', minval = 20, maxval = 756, display = display.none, group = "Signal: O''Neil Inspired: hi-percentile sb")
iOneilEpsYearsCheck = input.int(3, title = 'Eps years check', minval = 1, maxval = 5, display = display.none, group = "Signal: O''Neil Inspired: hi-percentile sb")
iOneilMinPercentileAvg = input.float(65, title = 'Min. percentile average', minval = 50, maxval = 99, display = display.none, group = "Signal: O''Neil Inspired: hi-percentile sb")
oiObvPercentile = ta.percentrank(ta.obv, iOneilPercentileLookback)
oiRsPercentile = ta.percentrank(rs, iOneilPercentileLookback)
totalShares1M = syminfo.shares_outstanding_total / 1000000.0
epsAct1M = request.earnings(ticker = syminfo.tickerid, field = earnings.actual) / totalShares1M
oiEpsPercentile = ta.percentrank(epsAct1M, iOneilEpsYearsCheck * 252)
epsChanges = countChanges(epsAct1M, iOneilEpsYearsCheck * 252)
oiPercentileAvg = math.avg(oiObvPercentile, oiRsPercentile, oiEpsPercentile)
oiPercentilesOkAgo = ta.barssince(oiPercentileAvg > (100 + iOneilMinPercentileAvg) / 2)
wonHpSb = oiPercentileAvg > iOneilMinPercentileAvg and oiPercentilesOkAgo < 50 and (rmv1Cond or rmv2Cond or rmv3Cond) and epsChanges > 3 * iOneilEpsYearsCheck and strongBreakout

//William O''Neil Inspired: turnaround GO: usually for general market turnaround
iTurnaroundExtremeAgo = input.int(defval = 45, title = "max. peak/bottom ago", minval = 20, maxval = 60, step = 5, display = display.none, group = "Signal: O''Neil Inspired: turnaround and GO")
iturnaroundGoDayMinRange = input.float(defval = 0.0, title = "min. day range", minval = 0.0, maxval = 10.0, step = 0.1, display = display.none, group = "Signal: O''Neil Inspired: turnaround and GO", tooltip = "Use 0 for auto calculation based on adr. \nfor adr < 0.017 uses 0.017\nfor adr >= 0.017 uses 0.017 + (adr - 0.017) / 4")
iTurnaroundMinGoDays = input.int(defval = 3, title = "min. days", minval = 1, maxval = 10, display = display.none, group = "Signal: O''Neil Inspired: turnaround and GO")

adr = adrPct / 100
turnaroundGoDayMinRange = iturnaroundGoDayMinRange > 0.0 ? iturnaroundGoDayMinRange / 100 : (adr < 0.017 ? 0.017 : 0.017 + (adr - 0.017) / 4)

wonTurnGoUp = drelib.sigWONTurnaroundUp(iTurnaroundExtremeAgo, iTurnaroundMinGoDays, turnaroundGoDayMinRange, mainMa, gVol50Ma)

// Riding AVWAP - touch and go (relay: majorLow → minorLow1 → minorLow2 → minorLow3)
iRidingVwapMajorLowLookup = input.int(defval = 150, title = "major low lookup", minval = 50, maxval = 300, display = display.none, group = "Signal: Riding Vwap TouchAndGo")
iRidingVwapLowsBelow = input.int(defval = 5, title = "Max. lows below vwap", minval = 1, maxval = 10, display = display.none, group = "Signal: Riding Vwap TouchAndGo")
iRidingVwapMaxTouchesPerVwap = input.int(defval = 2, title = 'Max. touches per Vwap', minval = 1, maxval = 5, display = display.none, group = "Signal: Riding Vwap TouchAndGo")
iRidingVwapNoTouchCancelThreshold = input.int(defval = 300, title = 'Vwap no touch cancel threshold', minval = 20, maxval = 500, step = 20, display = display.none, group = "Signal: Riding Vwap TouchAndGo")
iRidingVwapMinLowestCandle = input.int(defval = 10, title = 'Min. number of candles to check local low', minval = 3, maxval = 20, display = display.none, group = "Signal: Riding Vwap TouchAndGo")
iRidingVwapObvCond = input.bool(defval = true, title = 'Include above OBV cond.', display = display.none, group = "Signal: Riding Vwap TouchAndGo")
iRidingVwapVolCond = input.bool(defval = true, title = 'Require volume > SMA(30) on touch', display = display.none, group = "Signal: Riding Vwap TouchAndGo")
iRidingVwapContractionCond = input.bool(defval = false, title = 'Require contraction (RMV)', display = display.none, group = "Signal: Riding Vwap TouchAndGo")
iRidingVwapLowFlushCond = input.bool(defval = true, title = 'Low flush', display = display.none, group = "Signal: Riding Vwap TouchAndGo")
iRidingVwapRisingMainMaCond = input.bool(defval = true, title = 'Rising main MA', display = display.none, group = "Signal: Riding Vwap TouchAndGo")
iRidingVwapSrc = input.string(defval = "low", title = "VWAP price source", options = ["low", "high", "close", "ohlc4"], display = display.none, group = "Signal: Riding Vwap TouchAndGo")
ridingVwapSrc = switch iRidingVwapSrc
    "low"   => low
    "high"  => high
    "close" => close
    "ohlc4" => ohlc4
ridingVwapVolOk = iRidingVwapVolCond and volume > gVolMa or not iRidingVwapVolCond
contractionAgo = ta.barssince(lowRmv1 or lowRmv2 or lowRmv3)
ridingVwapContractionCond = iRidingVwapContractionCond and contractionAgo <= 2 or not iRidingVwapContractionCond
ridngVwapLowFlush = volume > gVolMa and volume > volume[1] or volume > 2 * gVolMa
ridngVwapLowFlushCond = iRidingVwapLowFlushCond and ridngVwapLowFlush or not iRidingVwapLowFlushCond
ridingVwapRisingMainMaCond = iRidingVwapRisingMainMaCond and mainMa > mainMa[1] or not iRidingVwapRisingMainMaCond
loweringMa = ta.barssince(mainMa < mainMa[1])
lowest200 = ta.lowest(iRidingVwapMajorLowLookup)
lowestSinceInception = ta.lowest(math.min(bar_index + 1, 500))
newStockMajorLow = low == lowestSinceInception and bar_index + 1 < iRidingVwapMajorLowLookup and bar_index + 1 > 10
majorLow = (low == lowest200 and loweringMa < 50 and low < mainMa) or newStockMajorLow
majorLVwap = ta.vwap(ridingVwapSrc, majorLow)
majorLowAgo = ta.barssince(majorLow)
majorLowVwap = majorLowAgo > iRidingVwapNoTouchCancelThreshold ? na : majorLVwap
lowsBelowMjVwap = math.sum(low < majorLVwap ? 1 : 0, 10)
vwapTouch = majorLowAgo > 10 and majorLowAgo < iRidingVwapNoTouchCancelThreshold and drelib.crossover(majorLVwap) and lowsBelowMjVwap <= iRidingVwapLowsBelow and ridingVwapVolOk and ridngVwapLowFlushCond[majorLowAgo]
lowestRecent = ta.lowest(iRidingVwapMinLowestCandle)

nextVwapTouch(series float _prevVWap, series float _src, int _prevLowsMinAgo) =>
    var int touchCount = 0
    newLow = low < _prevVWap and lowestRecent == low and _prevLowsMinAgo > 0
    lVwap = ta.vwap(_src, newLow)
    ago = ta.barssince(newLow)
    agedNewLowVwap = ago > _prevLowsMinAgo or ago > iRidingVwapNoTouchCancelThreshold ? na : lVwap
    lowsBelowLVwap = math.sum(low < agedNewLowVwap ? 1 : 0, 10)
    prevVwapTouch = drelib.crossover(_prevVWap) and lowsBelowLVwap <= iRidingVwapLowsBelow and touchCount <= iRidingVwapMaxTouchesPerVwap and ridngVwapLowFlushCond[_prevLowsMinAgo] and ridingVwapRisingMainMaCond
    touchCount := prevVwapTouch ? touchCount + 1 : touchCount
    [newLow, ago, agedNewLowVwap, prevVwapTouch]

[minorLow1, minorLow1Ago, minorLow1Vwap, vwapTouch2] = nextVwapTouch(majorLowVwap, ridingVwapSrc, majorLowAgo)
[minorLow2, minorLow2Ago, minorLow2Vwap, vwapTouch3] = nextVwapTouch(minorLow1Vwap, ridingVwapSrc, math.min(majorLowAgo, minorLow1Ago))
[minorLow3, minorLow3Ago, minorLow3Vwap, vwapTouch4] = nextVwapTouch(minorLow2Vwap, ridingVwapSrc, math.min(majorLowAgo, minorLow1Ago, minorLow2Ago))
[minorLow4, minorLow4Ago, minorLow4Vwap, vwapTouch5] = nextVwapTouch(minorLow3Vwap, ridingVwapSrc, math.min(majorLowAgo, minorLow1Ago, minorLow2Ago, minorLow3Ago))
[minorLow5, minorLow5Ago, minorLow5Vwap, vwapTouch6] = nextVwapTouch(minorLow4Vwap, ridingVwapSrc, math.min(majorLowAgo, minorLow1Ago, minorLow2Ago, minorLow3Ago, minorLow4Ago))
[minorLow6, minorLow6Ago, minorLow6Vwap, vwapTouch7] = nextVwapTouch(minorLow5Vwap, ridingVwapSrc, math.min(majorLowAgo, minorLow1Ago, minorLow2Ago, minorLow3Ago, minorLow4Ago, minorLow5Ago))

minVwapTAG = (
    ((vwapTouch or vwapTouch2) and not (vwapTouch3 or vwapTouch4 or vwapTouch5 or vwapTouch6 or vwapTouch7))
or ((vwapTouch2 or vwapTouch3) and not (vwapTouch or vwapTouch4 or vwapTouch5 or vwapTouch6 or vwapTouch7))
or ((vwapTouch3 or vwapTouch4) and not (vwapTouch or vwapTouch2 or vwapTouch5 or vwapTouch6 or vwapTouch7))
or ((vwapTouch4 or vwapTouch5) and not (vwapTouch or vwapTouch2 or vwapTouch3 or vwapTouch6 or vwapTouch7))
or ((vwapTouch5 or vwapTouch6) and not (vwapTouch or vwapTouch2 or vwapTouch3 or vwapTouch4 or vwapTouch7))
or ((vwapTouch6 or vwapTouch7) and not (vwapTouch or vwapTouch2 or vwapTouch3 or vwapTouch4 or vwapTouch5))
) and close >= high[1] and (iRidingVwapObvCond and obvCondRaw or not iRidingVwapObvCond) and ridingVwapVolOk and ridingVwapContractionCond

//Capitulation Low - highest volume on lowest point
iCapLowLowLookback = input.int(defval = 200, title = "major low lookback", minval = 50, maxval = 300, step = 5, display = display.none, group = "Signal: Capitulation Low")
iCapLowVolLookback = input.int(defval = 150, title = "Volume percentile lookback", minval = 50, maxval = 300, step = 5, display = display.none, group = "Signal: Capitulation Low")
iCapLowMinVolPercentile = input.int(defval = 95, title = "Volume percentile", minval = 50, maxval = 100, display = display.none, group = "Signal: Capitulation Low")
iCapLow2ndDayVolumeAboveAvg = input.bool(defval = true, title = '2nd day vol > avg', display = display.none, group = "Signal: Capitulation Low")
iCapLow2ndDayCloseGtThirdPrevCandle = input.bool(defval = false, title = '2nd day above prev. candles 1/3 height', display = display.none, group = "Signal: Capitulation Low")
iCapLow2ndDayHighAbovePrevHigh = input.bool(defval = true, title = '2nd day high above prev. high', display = display.none, group = "Signal: Capitulation Low")
lowestPrice = ta.lowest(iCapLowLowLookback)
volPercentile = ta.percentrank(volume, iCapLowVolLookback)
lphv = low == lowestPrice and volPercentile >= iCapLowMinVolPercentile
capLow2ndDayVolCond = iCapLow2ndDayVolumeAboveAvg and volume > gVolMa and volume > volume[1] / 3 or not iCapLow2ndDayVolumeAboveAvg
capLow2ndDayCandleCond = iCapLow2ndDayCloseGtThirdPrevCandle and close > low[1] + (high[1] - low[1]) / 3 or not iCapLow2ndDayCloseGtThirdPrevCandle
calLow2ndDayHighCond = iCapLow2ndDayHighAbovePrevHigh and high > high[1] or not iCapLow2ndDayHighAbovePrevHigh
CapLow = (lphv[1] or lphv) and low > low[1] and capLow2ndDayVolCond and capLow2ndDayCandleCond and calLow2ndDayHighCond


//Flat Breakout
iFlatBreakoutMinRecentPercentile = input.int(defval = 100, title = "Min. percentile", minval = 80, maxval = 100, step = 1, display = display.none, group = "Signal: Flat Breakout")
iFlatBreakoutClosesJumped = input.int(defval = 3, title = "Number of closes jumped", minval = 2, maxval = 50, step = 1, display = display.none, group = "Signal: Flat Breakout")
iFlatBreakoutMaxPercentileOverSMA200 = input.int(defval = 90, title = "Max percentile over sma200", minval = 5, maxval = 100, step = 5, display = display.none, group = "Signal: Flat Breakout")
var int FBLookback = 200
fBPercentRank = ta.percentrank(close, FBLookback)

dttVol = volume / gVolMa
dttVolTimePct = 100 * dttVol / dttTime
//math.pow(1-x, n) gives a nice concave function in x={0, 1} range, the bigger the n the more concave function is
dayEndMinVolumePct = 145
timeSinceSessionOpenAdditionalVolPct = math.pow(1 - dttTime, 5) * (iInitialMinVolumePct - dayEndMinVolumePct)
initialFlat = 0.01
volumeGood = (dttTime >= initialFlat ? (dttVolTimePct > dayEndMinVolumePct + timeSinceSessionOpenAdditionalVolPct) : volume > initialFlat * iInitialMinVolumePct * gVolMa) or volume > dayEndMinVolumePct * gVolMa

fbHighest = ta.highest(close, FBLookback)
fbRankCond = fBPercentRank == iFlatBreakoutMinRecentPercentile and fBPercentRank[1] <= (iFlatBreakoutMinRecentPercentile - iFlatBreakoutClosesJumped)
fbPercentileOverSma200 = ta.percentrank((close - mainMa) / mainMa, 200)
fbPercentileOverSmaCond = fbPercentileOverSma200[1] < iFlatBreakoutMaxPercentileOverSMA200
fb = fbRankCond and fbHighest[1] == fbHighest[6] and volumeGood and fbPercentileOverSmaCond

//VIP (Volume Instituional Push)
iVIPMaxPercentileOverSMA200 = input.int(defval = 50, title = "Max percentile over sma200", minval = 10, maxval = 100, step = 10, display = display.none, group = "Signal: Volume Institutional Push")
iVIPMin1DayVeryHighVol = input.bool(defval = false, title = 'min. 1 day of very high volume', display = display.none, group = "Signal: Volume Institutional Push")

vipDayGood = volume > gVolMa and close >= close[1]
vipDayGood_10 = vipDayGood ? 1 : 0
vipDayGood4 = math.sum(vipDayGood_10, 4)
vipDayGood6 = math.sum(vipDayGood_10, 6)
vip44 = vipDayGood4 == 4
vip44New = nz(ta.barssince(vip44[1]), 50) > 10 and vip44
vip56 = vipDayGood6 >= 5
vip56New = nz(ta.barssince(vip56[1]), 50) > 10 and vip56
vipHasEnoughBars = bar_index >= 200
vipPercentRankCond = not vipHasEnoughBars or fBPercentRank <= iVIPMaxPercentileOverSMA200
vipVHighVol = volume > 2 * gVolMa and close >= close[1]
vipVHighVol_10 = vipVHighVol ? 1 : 0
vipVHighVolCount = math.sum(vipVHighVol_10, 6)
vipVHighVolCountOk = vipVHighVolCount >= 1
vipRecentVHighVolCond = iVIPMin1DayVeryHighVol and vipVHighVolCountOk or not iVIPMin1DayVeryHighVol
vip = (vip44New or vip56New) and vipPercentRankCond and vipRecentVHighVolCond

//Qullamaggie EP: gap up + volume + base breakout; three parameter sets
baseHigh20 = ta.highest(high, 20)[1]
baseHigh50 = ta.highest(high, 50)[1]
epDttTime = drelib.dttTimePct()

epCalc(int _gapMin, float _volMin, float _closeLocMin, int _baseLookback, bool _requireGreen) =>
    float _gapPct = 100.0 * (open - close[1]) / close[1]
    float _barRange = high - low
    float _closeLoc = _barRange > 0 ? (close - low) / _barRange : 0.0
    float _dayEndPct = _volMin * 100.0
    float _initialPct = 2.0 * _dayEndPct
    float _dttVol = gVol50Ma > 0 ? volume / gVol50Ma : 0.0
    float _dttVolTimePct = 100.0 * _dttVol / math.max(epDttTime, 0.01)
    float _volAdditional = math.pow(1.0 - epDttTime, 5.0) * (_initialPct - _dayEndPct)
    float _baseHigh = _baseLookback == 20 ? baseHigh20 : baseHigh50
    bool _gapOk = _gapPct >= _gapMin
    bool _volOk = (epDttTime >= 0.01 ? _dttVolTimePct >= _dayEndPct + _volAdditional : volume >= 0.01 * _initialPct / 100.0 * gVol50Ma) or volume >= _dayEndPct / 100.0 * gVol50Ma
    bool _closeOk = _closeLoc >= _closeLocMin
    bool _baseOk = close > _baseHigh
    bool _ma50Ok = close > shortMa
    bool _ma200Ok = close > mainMa
    bool _sma50RiseOk = shortMa > shortMa[5]
    bool _greenOk = not _requireGreen or close > open
    _gapOk and _volOk and _closeOk and _baseOk and _ma50Ok and _ma200Ok and _sma50RiseOk and _greenOk

qulEp2 = epCalc(10, 2.0, 0.50, 50, true)
qulEp3 = epCalc(8, 1.5, 0.90, 20, false)

//Qullamaggie HTF: simplified htfCalc with five exposed parameters
htfSma10 = ta.sma(close, 10)
htfSma20 = ta.sma(close, 20)
htfSma50 = shortMa
htfMaAlign = close > htfSma10 and htfSma10 > htfSma20 and htfSma20 > htfSma50 and htfSma50 > htfSma50[5]
htfTightOk = (ta.highest(high, 5)[1] - ta.lowest(low, 5)[1]) < 0.8 * (ta.highest(high, 10)[6] - ta.lowest(low, 10)[6])
htfHigherLowsOk = ta.lowest(low, 5)[1] > ta.lowest(low, 10)[6]

//fixed 10-session flag and 80/40-session pole, as in the I2 HTF study
float htfBaseHigh = high[1]
float htfBaseHighClose = close[1]
float htfBaseLow = low[1]
for _i = 1 to 10
    htfBaseHigh := math.max(htfBaseHigh, high[_i])
    htfBaseHighClose := math.max(htfBaseHighClose, close[_i])
    htfBaseLow := math.min(htfBaseLow, low[_i])
int htfPoleStart = 11
int htfPoleEnd = math.min(90, bar_index)
float htfPolePeak = high[htfPoleStart]
int htfPeakOff = htfPoleStart
for _i = htfPoleStart to htfPoleEnd
    if high[_i] > htfPolePeak
        htfPolePeak := high[_i]
        htfPeakOff := _i
float htfPoleLow = low[htfPeakOff + 1]
int htfTroughOff = htfPeakOff + 1
int htfTroughEnd = math.min(htfPeakOff + 40, bar_index)
for _i = htfPeakOff + 1 to htfTroughEnd
    if low[_i] < htfPoleLow
        htfPoleLow := low[_i]
        htfTroughOff := _i
float htfPoleRet = 100.0 * (htfPolePeak / htfPoleLow - 1.0)
int htfPoleBars = htfTroughOff - htfPeakOff
float htfPullback = 100.0 * (htfPolePeak - htfBaseLow) / htfPolePeak
float htfBaseRange = 100.0 * (htfBaseHigh - htfBaseLow) / htfBaseHigh

//simplified factory: only the five parameters used by the Qul:HTF rows
htfCalc(float _breakoutMarginPct, float _maxPullbackPct, float _maxBaseRangePct, bool _useClosePivot, float _minCloseLoc) =>
    float _pivot = _useClosePivot ? htfBaseHighClose : htfBaseHigh
    float _barRange = high - low
    float _closeLoc = _barRange > 0 ? (close - low) / _barRange : 0.0
    bool _poleOk = not na(htfPoleRet) and htfPoleRet >= 50 and not na(htfPoleBars) and htfPoleBars >= 5
    bool _pullbackOk = not na(htfPullback) and htfPullback >= 0 and htfPullback <= _maxPullbackPct
    bool _rangeOk = not na(htfBaseRange) and htfBaseRange <= _maxBaseRangePct
    bool _structureOk = htfTightOk and htfHigherLowsOk
    bool _maOk = htfMaAlign
    bool _breakoutOk = not na(_pivot) and close > _pivot * (1.0 + _breakoutMarginPct / 100.0) and _closeLoc >= _minCloseLoc and volume > 1.5 * gVol50Ma
    _poleOk and _pullbackOk and _rangeOk and _structureOk and _maOk and _breakoutOk

//Qul:HTF = i2_margin3 (3% breakout margin, 25% pullback)
//Qul:HTF2 = i2_margin1_pb33 (1% breakout margin, 33% pullback)
qulHtf = htfCalc(3.0, 25.0, 25.0, false, 0.50)
qulHtf2 = htfCalc(1.0, 33.0, 25.0, false, 0.50)

//check performance
iShowSigPerfTable = input.bool(defval = false, title = 'show table', display = display.none, group = 'Sig. performance check')
iShowOnlyGoodSigs = input.bool(defval = true, title = 'show only good sigs.', display = display.none, group = 'Sig. performance check')
iUseQualityGate = input.bool(defval = false, title = 'use extended quality gate', display = display.none, group = 'Sig. performance check')
iMinSigCount = input.int(defval = 30, title = 'min. signals count', minval = 0, display = display.none, group = 'Sig. performance check')
iMinSigWilsonLb = input.float(defval = 30.0, title = 'min. win-rate lower bound (Wilson) [pct]', minval = 0.0, maxval = 100.0, step = 1.0, display = display.none, group = 'Sig. performance check')

showRow(_iShowOnlyGoodSigs, sigOk) =>
    _iShowOnlyGoodSigs and sigOk or not _iShowOnlyGoodSigs

showRow(_iShowOnlyGoodSigs, sigOk, _showThisSig) =>
    _showThisSig and (_iShowOnlyGoodSigs and sigOk or not _iShowOnlyGoodSigs)

float sl = math.max(ta.lowest(iSigStopLossDay + 1), close * (1.0 - iSigStopLossMaxPct / 100.0)) // max loss capped by higher of: current or prev. day low OR max % loss
[et3sbSuccRate, et3sbSuccCount, et3sbSigCount, et3sbAvgReturn, et3sbSuccRateOk, et3sbSuccRateStr, et3sbWinRate, et3sbWinCount, et3sbAvgR, et3sbMedR, et3sbStdR, et3sbPf, et3sbWilsonLb, et3sbAvgMfe, et3sbAvgMae, et3sbMaxDd, et3sbMaxLossStreak, et3sbScore, et3sbQualityOk, et3sbSumWinR, et3sbSumLossR] = dreperf.signalQualityFull(et3sb, sl, true, iMinSigSuccessRate, adrCond, iSigCheckTime, iMinSigCount, iMinSigWilsonLb)
